{"name":"Naked Noodle","hex":"#f7cb6e","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"naked","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bare, not covered by clothing.","Lacking some clothing; clothed only in underwear."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of nake"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/naked"},{"term":"noodle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A string or flat strip of pasta or other dough, usually cooked (at least initially) by boiling, and served in soup or in a dry form mixed with a sauce and other ingredients.","An object which is long and thin like a noodle (sense 1)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person with poor judgment; a fool.","The brain; the head."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/noodle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Noodles","blocks":[{"text":"Noodles are a type of food typically made from unleavened dough which is rolled flat and cut, stretched, or extruded into long strips or strings. Noodles are a staple food in many cultures and made into a variety of shapes. The most common noodles are those derived from Chinese cuisine or Italian cuisine. Italian noodles are generally referred to as pasta. In Chinese cuisine, the overarching term for noodles is 麵, which refers specifically to dough-based noodles made from wheat or other grain-based dough. Chinese noodles also include another category, called 粉 (fěn), which are not made by kneading dough but from a starch slurry, such as rice noodles, and cellophane noodles. These are not made from wheat dough, but are still regarded as noodles in English due to their physical form and culinary role."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Dalian_Liaoning_China_Noodlemaker-01.jpg/330px-Dalian_Liaoning_China_Noodlemaker-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Noodles"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Dalian_Liaoning_China_Noodlemaker-01.jpg/500px-Dalian_Liaoning_China_Noodlemaker-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Dalian_Liaoning_China_Noodlemaker-01.jpg/1280px-Dalian_Liaoning_China_Noodlemaker-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Dalian_Liaoning_China_Noodlemaker-01.jpg/500px-Dalian_Liaoning_China_Noodlemaker-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADalian_Liaoning_China_Noodlemaker-01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Bun_thit_nuong.jpg/500px-Bun_thit_nuong.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Bun_thit_nuong.jpg/1280px-Bun_thit_nuong.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Bun_thit_nuong.jpg/500px-Bun_thit_nuong.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A bowl of Bún thịt nướng","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABun_thit_nuong.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Vermeer_van_Utrecht_Man_eating_noodels.JPG/500px-Vermeer_van_Utrecht_Man_eating_noodels.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Vermeer_van_Utrecht_Man_eating_noodels.JPG/500px-Vermeer_van_Utrecht_Man_eating_noodels.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jan Vermeer van Utrecht's painting of a man eating unspecified noodles (National Museum, Warsaw)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVermeer_van_U